  "findings": [
    {
      "pages": [
        2,
        3,
        4,
        5,
        6
      ],
      "finding": "Targets prefill with static graph preparation and fixed prompt chunks. Weight-bearing subgraphs are shared across attention shapes; physical unified memory still has runtime buffers, copies and synchronization."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        6,
        7,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "finding": "INT8 per-tensor matmul uses CPU floating-point attention/normalization and shadow outlier work. Chunk scheduling retains dependency legality and optimizes the busy resource; pruning shadow work has a quality condition."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "finding": "Implemented system uses CPU+NPU and CPU decode. Models are historical 1.8–7B configurations on Snapdragon 8 Gen2/3 phones. Long-input short-output task results cannot establish long-output end-to-end gains; PowerInferV2 numbers were taken from its paper."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        12,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "finding": "Accuracy changes are task/model-specific. GPU+NPU evaluation is simulation rather than an implemented GPU runtime. Some table arithmetic, plotted task labels and phone-name references differ; do not adopt headline speedups or a uniform accuracy bound."
    },
    {
      "pages": [
        15
      ],
      "finding": "Artifact appendix covers prefill performance and accuracy sections, not every experiment. It calls for an A100 server and Redmi K70 Pro; Qwen1.5-1.8B is the example. Zenodo access failed twice in this phase; no artifact execution."
    }
  ],
